{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 9, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a biographical drama film directed by david fincher and written by the screenplay duo of jesse eisenberg and aaron sorkin. the movie is based on the true story of the founding of the social networking site facebook and the subsequent lawsuits that followed.\n\nthe film stars jesse eisenberg as mark zuckerberg, the founder of facebook, alongside joshua jackson as sean parker, a key figure in the development of the site. the movie also features a talented ensemble cast, including andrew garfield as eduardo saverin, the site's first investor, and armie hammer as cambridge university student andrew mcnally, who was a key figure in the development of the site.\n\none of the standout aspects of the social network is its portrayal of the cutthroat world of silicon valley. the movie delves into the cutthroat world of college students and their obsession with technology and innovation. the film also explores the darker side of ambition and the consequences of success.\n\nthe cinematography in the social network is stunning, with david fincher using a muted color palette to reflect the bleak and isolated world of the characters. the film's score, composed by trent reznor and atticus ross, is equally impressive, using a mix of electronic and orchestral elements to create a haunting and atmospheric sound.\n\njessie eisenberg's performance as mark zuckerberg is particularly noteworthy, as he captures the character's awkwardness and intensity with ease. joshua jackson's portrayal of sean parker is also excellent, bringing a sense of charm and charisma to the role.\n\naaron sorkin's screenplay is also a highlight of the film, as he expertly weaves together the complex web of relationships and lawsuits that defined the early days of facebook. sorkin's dialogue is sharp and witty, with many memorable lines that have become ingrained in popular culture.\n\noverall, the social network is a gripping and thought-provoking film that offers a unique perspective on the world of technology and innovation. with its talented cast, stunning cinematography, and sharp screenplay, it's a must-see for anyone interested in the world of social media and the people who shape it.\n\ngrade: a-\n\nrating: 9.5/10\n\nrecommendation: if you enjoy biographical dramas, technology, or innovation, you'll love the social network. it's also a great choice for anyone interested in the world of social media and the people who shape it. however, be warned: the film does contain some mature themes and language, so viewer discretion is advised.", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -0.045232724}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -0.0016868184}, {"token": " network", "logprob": -7.6293654e-06}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.18040486}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.00012385078}, {"token": " bi", "logprob": -1.8251517}, {"token": "ographical", "logprob": -0.00014363688}, {"token": " drama", "logprob": -0.0063425205}, {"token": " film", "logprob": -0.0024567442}, {"token": " directed", "logprob": -1.0097208}, {"token": " by", "logprob": -0.0015062665}, {"token": " david", "logprob": -0.009424718}, {"token": " fin", "logprob": -0.00040570612}, {"token": "cher", "logprob": -4.005352e-05}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.9112628}, {"token": " written", "logprob": -0.1821079}, {"token": " by", "logprob": -2.7418098e-06}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -2.9088922}, {"token": " screenplay", "logprob": -1.1487632}, {"token": " duo", "logprob": -0.53453386}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.1280681}, {"token": " j", "logprob": -0.6768376}, {"token": "esse", "logprob": -0.042398397}, {"token": " e", "logprob": -0.08598238}, {"token": "isen", "logprob": -0.0008628221}, {"token": "berg", "logprob": -1.5139465e-05}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.15123203}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -1.8688097}, {"token": "aron", "logprob": -0.000981207}, {"token": " s", 